<title>USA: Security Capital debt rating raised.</title>
<headline>Security Capital debt rating raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Tuesday it raised its rating on Security Capital Industrial Trust, an owner of industrial properties, to single-A-minus from triple-B-plus.</p>
<p>The upgrade is based on Duff &amp; Phelp's increasing comfort level with Security Capital's acquisition, development and management track record, the credit rating agency said.  </p>
<p>The rating change, which also takes in to account the company's plan to expand into European markets, affects $625 million in notes, Duff &amp; Phelps said.</p>
<p>Security Capital shares were unchanged at 21-1/2 Tuesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
